WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.440
Introduce yourself in French
and you say «Je m'appelle Sam».

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.020
Word for word, that's 'I call myself Sam'.

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.200
Who calls themselves anything?

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.490
It gets stranger.

5
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.370
French can say the same
word twice in a row:

6
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.470
«nous nous lavons».

7
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:16.930
Is that a typo?

8
00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.730
And with one small word,

9
00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.990
«Ils se regardent» means
'they look at each other'.

10
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.860
So why does French say 'I call myself Sam'

11
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.670
when English just says 'My name is Sam'?

12
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.420
In this mission, you'll ride
the pronoun train and pin

13
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.540
a day's routine to the clock.

14
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.230
Then you'll split 'self'
from 'each other',

15
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.780
and build your own sentences in the lab.

16
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.030
Your mission: find out why French
needs that extra little word.
